winemac-ascii-keyboard-layout.patch - Gamify patch over CrossOver 25.1.0 Wine (dlls/winemac.drv), LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Found with Wolfenstein II: The New Colossus (Steam 612880, idTech 6.5) on a Mac with the Hebrew layout
selected. The game resolves its key bindings by key name through the active layout; on Hebrew no key
types "w", so `bind "W" "_moveforward"` (and A, S, D, R) were dropped and the game saved its bindings
without them; its prompts showed "*" for every letter key. DirectInput still got the right scan codes.
 Mac Driver option ASCIIKeyboardLayout ("y"/"n", off by default; Gamify's `latinLayout` setting turns
 it on): while the selected keyboard layout is not ASCII-capable (kTISPropertyInputSourceIsASCIICapable:
 Hebrew, Russian, Greek, Arabic...), Windows programs get TISCopyCurrentASCIICapableKeyboardLayoutInputSource()
 (ABC, U.S. ...) for key mapping, ToUnicode and the HKL; ASCII-capable layouts (AZERTY, QWERTZ...) are
 kept. An HKL that the input source list does not know (that layout not enabled) falls back to 0x04090409.
 Typing non-Latin text inside Windows programs needs the option off.
Apply: patch -p1 -d upstream/crossover-sources-25.1.0/sources/wine < src/patches/winemac-ascii-keyboard-layout.patch

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_cocoa.h
